Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:58:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Admit recovered mechanisms to the docket: the novel-mechanism
 lane ended one line short

A MECHANISM WITH NO REGISTERED FAMILY FUNCTION REACHES THE JUDGE BY EXACTLY ONE ROUTE. The
compiler's deterministic vocabulary refuses it by name -- NEEDS_EXACT_RULE_EXTRACTION -- and
`deepening_worker` then spends a model call recovering the rule from the row's own text,
re-running the recovery through `compile_row` so no admission guard is bypassed. Everything else
the desk mines is a REGISTERED family being re-parameterised, so that one route is how the
Chinese, Japanese, Korean and Russian forests, the championship records, the world crawler and the
arXiv feed contribute anything the desk did not already know.

ITS OUTPUT WAS READ BY NOBODY. `deepened_candidates.json` was rewritten every pass and consumed
only by `portfolio_gap` for gap ANALYSIS and by `convert_swarm` for a log line. It was not in
`merge_hypotheses.SOURCES`, and that tuple is what builds `external_survivors.json` -- the one
docket `external_gauntlet` opens. So every recovery stopped there.

WHAT KEPT IT INVISIBLE is the part worth recording. `libs/ops/capability_graph.py` asserted the
edge in as many words -- "deepened_candidates.json: external_gauntlet via compiler merge" -- and
a comment beside it calls "deepening_worker -> deepened_candidates -> external_gauntlet ... a real
path". The graph said the lane was connected; the graph was not the thing doing the connecting.
An edge the graph names and nothing implements is worse than a missing edge, because it stops
anyone looking (L1.49: a gate that never ran is a claim the desk cannot cash).

MEASURED ON THE TRADING BOX 2026-09-24: 83 mechanisms recovered in the worker's lifetime, 30 of
them in the preceding 24 hours, every one bought with the scarcest budget the desk owns -- one
OpenRouter account, 1,000 model requests a day, exhausted by 01:42 UTC. Not one had ever reached
the docket, so not one had ever been judged. The desk was spending its entire novel-mechanism
allowance into a file with no reader.

NOTHING IS RELAXED BY ADMITTING THEM. These rows come out of `compile_row` -- the same function
that produces miner_candidates' hypotheses -- so they are contract-identical by construction.
They face the identical ten gates, the same family routing, the same untradeable-symbol filter
and the same family-less drop as every other source in the tuple. The bars are untouched and
fixed_trial_count is unchanged; this adds arrivals, which is free, not leniency.

It also makes the lane ATTRIBUTABLE for the first time: the merge stamps `producer`, so
`certificate_provenance` can now answer whether a model-recovered mechanism has ever earned a
certificate -- a question that previously could not be ASKED, because no certificate could descend
from a row that never arrived.

The new test is deliberately CROSS-MODULE: it reads `deepening_worker.OUT` and the worker's own
output key rather than a literal string, so a rename on either side fails there instead of
silently reopening the hole. It also pins the capability-graph claim to the merge that implements
it.

